  "questionId": "t05-q02",
  "speechText": "The hard part is stale data after a database write. With cache-aside, I read Redis first, load the database on a miss, and cache the result with a TTL. After a successful update, I delete the related cache key so the next read reloads it. There is still a short race between a read and a write, so I would read the database directly when fresh data is required.",
